# Runner-image mapping for local `act` runs (see CONTRIBUTING.md
# "Running CI locally with act"). The catthehacker medium image ships
# the runner runtime the pinned action versions (checkout@v7,
# cache@v4, upload-artifact@v7, mise-action@v4) need — the default
# nektos/act-environments images are too small for them.
#
# macos-* labels map to the same Linux image: a local approximation for
# smoke-running workflow logic, NOT a faithful macOS environment (no
# macOS SDK, no Darwin behavior). The image is multi-arch — Docker
# pulls the native variant (arm64 on Apple Silicon), so the pinned zig
# toolchain mise installs inside the container is also native. Do NOT
# force --container-architecture linux/amd64 on Apple Silicon: Rosetta
# cannot run the zig compiler binary ("bss_size overflow").
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
-P ubuntu-24.04-arm=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
-P macos-14=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
-P macos-15=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
-P macos-26=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest